.SH BUGS
One timeline (home); no public/local/hashtag timelines, no search,
no media, no polls, no unfav/unboost/unfollow, no muting or
blocking, no GUI, and no abstraction shared with
.IR bsky (1)
(each is deliberately self-contained \(em see masto.b's own header
comment for why). The HTML stripper is a linear tag scan, not a real
parser, though it does track quoted attribute values so a literal
.B >
inside one no longer leaks markup. The write commands were verified
against the real server only up to authentication (a bogus token
draws the server's own decoded error); actually posting from a test
run would be spam, so the final acceptance path relies on
.B buildtest()
pinning the request bodies Mastodon documents.
